       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so the effects could last for days.\n\nTypical adult dosing:\n- **Hypertension or coronary artery disease:** start at 5 mg once daily, and titrate to a maximum of 10 mg once daily.\n- **Frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment:** start at 2.5 mg once daily.\n\nWas 5 mg the intended dose, with an extra zero by mistake? Or is there a clinical reason for a different dose? If you tell me the intended dose, I'll enter the order right away. Please also check with your resident or attending first if you're unsure."
