       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. Confirming the number doesn't change the safety problem. 50 mg daily is far above the 10 mg maximum, and I don't know of any indication for it in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. The risk is serious harm, and the order would go into the system looking routine.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Talk to your resident or attending.** If they want a dose above the labeled maximum for a specific reason, they can review it and enter it themselves. It should also be documented with the rationale and monitoring plan.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** They can check the dose and advise on whether it's appropriate.\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can do that now, for example 5 mg by mouth once daily, or 10 mg if more effect is needed.\n\nIf you tell me which standard dose you'd like, I'll enter it right away."
      }
